[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-54155"] :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x={t}^{2}-2,\\,y=2{t}^{4}+5$ where $t$ is a real number. Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=8{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{8{t}^{3}}{2t}=4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(4{t}^{2})}{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{8t}{2t} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-78951/selection/1d3d4e8e0e9c46650352092c2eb5fe5ffa82989aec4ce6d5b0c890d30189bfcd" :answer/id #uuid "b61d4ec9-d636-575f-839d-fb57453e40f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78951/selection/8ef5457e0d870c7ec97ce900e1fb3b54d670afe468ee97512968a01746334ce9" :answer/id #uuid "1f22d3a9-5228-5c1a-8a86-52ac286eb952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{csc}^{3}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78951/selection/7bd8f88a12c33d792084942a2e53c309e0f1ef514148e0051e0f1d88ecb36541" :answer/id #uuid "82f1333c-b8da-52c3-8a7b-8951e9938b3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{3}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78951/selection/b15e40ab8e8e18f331fb8eb9370a5822555efba95ce0dd8e3be761762c347430" :answer/id #uuid "7ef6a1ce-d92a-55ba-a777-e2106002860e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78951/selection/5400f9160a717923a8d7862697f36e49626bca2d07216ad6a63892c39dff1ce4" :answer/id #uuid "5f9a464b-1d2d-5e21-a52a-9403e0a68967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{csc}^{2}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78951/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "685815d1-1ed0-59c7-8ae3-f8a94d16c816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78951/selection/8ef5457e0d870c7ec97ce900e1fb3b54d670afe468ee97512968a01746334ce9" :answer-field/choices ["q-78951/selection/1d3d4e8e0e9c46650352092c2eb5fe5ffa82989aec4ce6d5b0c890d30189bfcd" "q-78951/selection/8ef5457e0d870c7ec97ce900e1fb3b54d670afe468ee97512968a01746334ce9" "q-78951/selection/7bd8f88a12c33d792084942a2e53c309e0f1ef514148e0051e0f1d88ecb36541" "q-78951/selection/b15e40ab8e8e18f331fb8eb9370a5822555efba95ce0dd8e3be761762c347430" "q-78951/selection/5400f9160a717923a8d7862697f36e49626bca2d07216ad6a63892c39dff1ce4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78951" :question/id #uuid "0e2cd58a-0e3a-5779-a922-6155d814596a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78951" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1.$ Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2{csc}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{3}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78951/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16dac5bd-acbd-51c6-8636-172e3a55aaf1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78951"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78959/selection/dbc9f34791df2cfa1ba97f4fcb508d6756c3df39f1458e13c2498bf0264679fe" :answer/id #uuid "134e90c1-5003-5221-9133-0c97e451aa70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78959/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "c0d4cd53-0fd9-5138-a845-0bd846cabd5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78959/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "d11506e5-c742-54bc-86a4-fe839a293dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78959/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "5f938462-6aa1-56e8-81d2-f0dda900629f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78959/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "27b10cda-c49f-54c7-8027-73c9dbe8e26a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78959/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "219a63ea-a8d7-5c77-98a4-568661cdc46c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78959/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer-field/choices ["q-78959/selection/dbc9f34791df2cfa1ba97f4fcb508d6756c3df39f1458e13c2498bf0264679fe" "q-78959/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-78959/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-78959/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-78959/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78959" :question/id #uuid "a54e1fd7-9935-5657-bbe7-304f383e1956" :question/math-academy-id "q-78959" :question/problem "A curve has parametric equations $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+4,\\,y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).$ Given that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t),$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t),$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+4)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t))}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{12{sec}^{2}⁡(3t)}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\  & =4{sec}^{3}⁡(3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{9},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}{|}_{t=\\pi /9} & =4{sec}^{3}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{cos}^{3}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78959/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fb50541-88df-5f3f-